From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:05:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screensaver mode: settings in memory, --screensaver, Esc,
 mouse to the plugin

A screensaver mode on the title screen (src/openrct2-ui/screensaver/):
entering closes the title windows and hides every other window but the park's own
(transparent and invisible, so the park is drawn under them; a new window flag, hidden,
keeps the per-tick visibility update from showing them again), and applies the mode's
settings in memory: window style (borderless by default), title music, game speed,
light effects and weather gloom off by default, and uncapped frames off, so the game
draws once per tick (40 fps). Config::SetSaveHook keeps them out of config.ini; leaving
restores the user's values and reopens the title menu.

--screensaver starts in the mode; Esc then quits. Entered from the menu, Esc leaves the
mode. While the mode is on, mouse moves, buttons and the wheel go to the plugin instead
of the windows.

Plugin API: the screensaver global (active, launchedByFlag, settings, cursorVisible,
enter, exit, configure, onChange, onMouse).
